def worst_chain(keys, capacity):
    counts = [0] * capacity
    for k in keys:
        counts[hash(k) % capacity] += 1
    return max(counts)

print(worst_chain(range(100), 64), worst_chain(range(0, 6400, 64), 64))
```
Every multiple of 64 has remainder 0, so all 100 keys share one bucket and every lookup scans 100 pairs: O(n). The hash function is fine; the problem is that the bucket index throws away all but the lowest bits, and these keys differ only in higher bits.

